    <!-- WHAT THERAPY LOOKS LIKE -->
    <section class="section dark-section" id="what-we-do">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">How The Work Moves</span>
        <h2>Evidence-based methods, no wasted time.</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">I use structured, well-researched approaches built to actually quiet anxiety, not open-ended talk that keeps you stuck in the worry. We start with what's fueling it, build tools you can use in real time, and keep it tied to your day-to-day life. Three methods anchor the work:</p>
        <div class="cards-3">
          <article class="card reveal">
            <span class="num">CBT</span>
            <h3>Break the worry loop</h3>
            <p class="method-sub">Cognitive Behavioral Therapy</p>
            <p>We find the thought patterns that feed the anxiety (the catastrophizing, the what-ifs, the need to be sure) and build practical ways to interrupt them. The gold-standard approach for anxiety, and it works.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card reveal">
            <span class="num">DBT</span>
            <h3>Settle the body in the moment</h3>
            <p class="method-sub">Dialectical Behavior Therapy</p>
            <p>Real tools for when anxiety spikes: racing heart, tight chest, panic rising. Skills to ground yourself fast so the moment doesn't run away with you.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card reveal">
            <span class="num">ACT</span>
            <h3>Stop fighting the thoughts</h3>
            <p class="method-sub">Acceptance &amp; Commitment Therapy</p>
            <p>Anxiety gets louder the harder you wrestle it. This work helps you loosen its grip and get back to living the life you want, instead of organizing everything around avoiding the worry.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

